# {{.ProjectName}}

A Rust application built with modern Rust practices, focusing on performance, safety, and maintainability.

## Prerequisites

- Rust 1.70.0 or higher
- Cargo (comes with Rust)

## Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone
cd {{.ProjectName}}

# Build the project
cargo build
```

## Usage

```bash
# Run the application
cargo run

# Run with arguments
cargo run -- --help

# Run a specific binary (if multiple)
cargo run --bin {{.ProjectName}}
```

## Development

```bash
# Check code without building
cargo check

# Run with optimizations (faster execution)
cargo run --release

# Watch for changes and rebuild automatically
cargo install cargo-watch
cargo watch -x run

# Format code
cargo fmt

# Lint code
cargo clippy
cargo clippy -- -D warnings  # Treat warnings as errors
```

## Building

```bash
# Debug build (default)
cargo build

# Release build (optimized)
cargo build --release

# Cross-compilation examples
cargo build --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu
cargo build --target x86_64-apple-darwin
cargo build --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu

# Build all targets
cargo build --all-targets
```

## Testing

```bash
# Run all tests
cargo test

# Run tests with output
cargo test -- --nocapture

# Run specific test
cargo test test_function_name

# Run integration tests only
cargo test --test integration_tests

# Run tests with coverage (requires cargo-tarpaulin)
cargo install cargo-tarpaulin
cargo tarpaulin --out html

# Benchmark tests
cargo test --release -- --ignored
```

## Benchmarking

```bash
# Run benchmarks (requires nightly Rust)
rustup install nightly
cargo +nightly bench

# Or using criterion (add to Cargo.toml)
cargo bench
```

